From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:29:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] core: Fire Emblem Fates: a mod's chapter person files
 served under their own archive name

Person::Serialize (0x0044AB60) writes the inner archive name of each loaded chapter
Person block into a battle save; Person::Deserialize (0x0044A0FC) loads
GameData/Person/<route>/<name>.bin.lz by that name. Every file of the game carries its
own file name; Seal of Flames v6's 41 new chapter person files kept the name of the file
they were copied from, so a battle save reloaded the original chapter's people (other
enemies, a black GameElapse screen, or the title). zakuro-fs gets a Fix hook over the
files a mod puts in (Layered::new_fixed, Title::lay_mods_fixed); zakuro-core's mods::lay
passes fates_person_name for the Fates title only: a same-length name in a mod's
GameData/Person file is set to the file's own stem, recompressed with an in-place LZ13
size. The installed mod is unchanged on disk; without a mods folder nothing runs
(docs/tests/SEAL_SAVE.md).
